            <ArticleTitle>Vertebroplasty: a simple solution to a difficult problem.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vertebroplasty is the percutaneous injection of bone cement into a symptomatic fractured vertebral body under fluoroscopic guidance. It is a safe and simple outpatient procedure. We discuss patient selection, the techniques, and the results based on our experience and that of our radiology colleagues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
